  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Daulat Singh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 10 September, 2024 Author: Dinesh Kumar Paliwal Bench: Dinesh Kumar Paliwal 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Crr No. 4402 of 2022 (Daulat Singh Vs The State Of Madhya Prades Dated : 10-09-2024 Shri Sankalp Kochar - Advocate for the applicant. Shri Aditya Gupta - Panel Lawyer for the respondent/Stat Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant has surrendered and he is in jail since 12.08.2024. Therefore, objection raised by the Registry is over ruled. Heard on I.A.No.23285/2024, second application under Section 389(1) of Cr.P.C/corresponding Section 430 of Bhartiya Nagrik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 for suspension of sentence and grant of bail to applicant.",
    "facts": "It is revision, therefore, provision of Section 389(1) of Cr.P.C and Section 430 of BNSS are not applicable. However, said default is ignored subject to payment of cost of Rs.10000/- in the M.P. High Court Bar Association Fund. Applicant was convicted for commission of offence under Sections 7(i) & 7(iii) read with Section 16(1)(A)(i) Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 by the learned JMFC, Khandwa (M.P.) vide judgment dated 03.11.2017 passed in RCT/800174/2011 (State of M.P. Vs. Daulat Singh).",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant has been erroneously convicted by both the Courts below as they have not taken into consideration the fact that on the date on which the offence alleged to have been committed Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 was not in force, the same has already been repealed by Food Safety Standard Act, 2006. Therefore, it was not justified for the Courts below to convict the applicant under the provisions of the repealed Act. He has fair chances Daulat Singh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 10 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/62855944/ 1 to succeed in revision."
  },
